&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is PawaPay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PawaPay is a pan-African fintech enabling local payment channels used by the mass market to both local and international merchants. We operate in a highly regulated, partner-driven environment and are in scale-up mode, with ambitious growth plans across multiple African markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to simplify business for companies and consumers in Africa and we do that by ensuring that payments simply work, at scale, despite fragmentation and complexity that exists on the Continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our payments API we already facilitate over 4 million transactions a day across 20 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa.&amp;nbsp; We are the largest PSP on the Continent for the processing of mobile money payments, and have positioned ourselves well to lead the payment space as it grows over the next decade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PawaPay, there is an entrepreneurial spirit coupled with a modern and professional working culture. The fast-paced, ever-changing environment will suit someone who can adapt and think on their feet. In return, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a group of dedicated and smart individuals working towards the same mission. We work as a remote team and have team members in Europe, Africa and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Country Director for Mali at PawaPay, you will lead the company’s operations and partner relationships within Mali. This role combines relationship management, business development execution, and operational oversight with core governance duties. You will support the execution of Group strategy locally, helping identify growth opportunities while ensuring that PawaPay delivers exceptional service levels and strong partner performance in the market.&lt;br&gt;You will work closely with cross-functional teams across Product, Sales, Operations, Compliance, Finance, and Legal, ensuring effective coordination and a seamless experience for our partners.&lt;br&gt;This position requires a proactive, strategic, and highly organised leader with excellent stakeholder management capability and a deep understanding of the mobile money and fintech ecosystem in Mali and the wider West African region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management.&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary relationship holder for all in-country partners (MMOs, banks, financial institutions). Lead ongoing engagement, service reviews, dispute resolution, and maintain strong local presence and responsiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Development &amp;amp; Commercial Engagement.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead initial commercial conversations with local partners, drive end-to-end onboarding/integration, identify product expansion opportunities, and generate local merchant leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; Own local issue resolution, manage local administrative/KYC requirements, oversee office operations, monitor operational KPIs, and maintain high service uptime with partner technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional In-Country Support.&lt;/strong&gt; Provide targeted local support to Group functions including Legal, Compliance/GRC, Finance/Tax, and People Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Representation.&lt;/strong&gt; Act as Company Director and bank signatory for the local entity, ensure statutory compliance, submit monthly/board reports, and represent PawaPay brand locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first 12 months, success in this role means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong In-Country Partner Relationships.&lt;/strong&gt; High-trust partnerships established with key local MMOs, banks, and regulators, backed by structured recurring service reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seamless Operations &amp;amp; Governance.&lt;/strong&gt; Full statutory and legal compliance across Mali, robust local banking controls, and high operational uptime across payment channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Growth.&lt;/strong&gt; Target partners successfully onboarded and live, alongside a steady pipeline of qualified local merchant leads for Group sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years in stakeholder management, business development, regulatory liaison, or operational leadership within fintech, mobile money, telecoms, or financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Stakeholder Management.&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record managing external relationships with regulators, mobile network operators, and banks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Proficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in English and French (local market requirements).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of the African payments and mobile money ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Economics, or related field; high integrity and proactive ownership mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or MBA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in cross-border regional expansion across neighbouring West African markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PawaPay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;_651c1b54 _6e226a26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve financial access in Africa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being part of an amazing team that shapes company’s culture as a great place to be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ambitious, talented, and diverse team who always has your back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We grow fast, and you will grow fast with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive remuneration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;35 days of paid leave per year (inclusive of public holidays) and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is PawaPay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PawaPay is a pan-African fintech enabling local payment channels used by the mass market to both local and international merchants. We operate in a highly regulated, partner-driven environment and are in scale-up mode, with ambitious growth plans across multiple African markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to simplify business for companies and consumers in Africa and we do that by ensuring that payments simply work, at scale, despite fragmentation and complexity that exists on the Continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our payments API we already facilitate over 4 million transactions a day across 20 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa.&amp;nbsp; We are the largest PSP on the Continent for the processing of mobile money payments, and have positioned ourselves well to lead the payment space as it grows over the next decade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PawaPay, there is an entrepreneurial spirit coupled with a modern and professional working culture. The fast-paced, ever-changing environment will suit someone who can adapt and think on their feet. In return, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a group of dedicated and smart individuals working towards the same mission. We work as a remote team and have team members in Europe, Africa and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The Country Operations Associate provides critical administrative, operational, and coordination support to the Country Director and relevant Group functions within the country. Acting as the operational backbone of the local business, the role ensures the seamless execution of day-to-day activities by managing documentation, tracking actions, coordinating meetings, supporting mobile network operator (MNO) engagements, administering contracts, assisting with compliance requirements and overseeing office administration.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The role enables the Country Director to focus on strategic priorities, senior partner relationships, governance, commercial opportunities, market performance and material escalations. The Country Administrator supports execution and follow-through but does not replace the Country Director’s responsibility for country leadership, strategy, senior stakeholder ownership, or governance responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;216&quot; data-end=&quot;295&quot;&gt;This role is open to Tanzanian nationals currently living in Tanzania only.&lt;/strong&gt; Applicants must be based in Tanzania and have the right to work in Tanzania.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you are accountable for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The single thing this role is accountable for is the operational backbone and execution of day-to-day administrative, partner, merchant, and compliance coordination in Tanzania.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating Principle: The Country Operations Associate coordinates, chases, documents, schedules, prepares, tracks, and follows up on agreed tasks. Strategic priorities, pricing, commercial terms, senior partner management, regulatory interpretation, legal risk, public representation, and material operational incidents belong to the Country Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;What you own day to day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management.&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the secondary relationship holder for in-country partners (MMOs, banks, financial institutions), especially when the Country Director is unavailable. Maintain partner satisfaction through regular engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative Support to Country Director.&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate meeting logistics, agendas, action trackers, briefing notes, status updates, and administrative records. Manage local office administration, vendors, lease renewals, and event logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Merchant Onboarding &amp;amp; KYC Administration.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare MNO approval requests, review merchant onboarding packs for completeness, coordinate follow-up between teams, and track onboarding status and blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wallet Operations &amp;amp; MNO Coordination.&lt;/strong&gt; Submit wallet user access and change requests, track wallet confirmations/credentials, act as the first point for routine MNO operational tasks, and notify key teams of material issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract, Legal &amp;amp; Document Execution Support.&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate signing workflows across MNOs, banks, and suppliers; maintain signing trackers; upload executed agreements to repositories; and escalate delays or legal concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance, Regulatory &amp;amp; Finance Administration.&lt;/strong&gt; Track local compliance cycles (tax clearance, licence renewals, filings), assist with document collection for audits and regulatory requests, and flag expiring licences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you do not own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Leadership &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt; — sits with the Country Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior External Stakeholder Ownership &amp;amp; Primary Relationship Holding&lt;/strong&gt; — sits with the Country Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial, Pricing &amp;amp; Legal Sign-Off&lt;/strong&gt; — sits with Country Director, Legal &amp;amp; Group Functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How the role is measured&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onboarding &amp;amp; Contract Cycle Times.&lt;/strong&gt; Speed and completeness of merchant KYC documentation and MNO submission tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative &amp;amp; Record Currency.&lt;/strong&gt; Timely upload and maintenance of executed contracts, licences, and compliance filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Responsiveness.&lt;/strong&gt; Timely follow-up and escalation of wallet requests, MNO operational issues, and office admin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Minimum 3 years of experience in administration, operations coordination, project coordination, partner support, banking, telecoms, fintech, payments, or a similar environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive Follow-Through.&lt;/strong&gt; Persistent in chasing open tasks and action items, with strong attention to detail and clear escalation boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tooling.&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of Google Workspace or Microsoft Office (Docs/Word, Sheets/Excel, Calendar, Email).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working with MNOs, banks, regulators, tax authorities, or fintech/payments stakeholders is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages.&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in English and Swahili/relevant local language(s).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote Work.&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable and experienced with working effectively in a remote team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational &amp;amp; Tracking Precision&lt;/strong&gt; — Ability to manage multiple trackers, deadlines, documents, and stakeholders simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Communication&lt;/strong&gt; — Clear, professional communication with external partners (MNOs, banks, regulators) and internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discretion &amp;amp; Confidentiality&lt;/strong&gt; — High level of integrity, confidentiality, and composure in a remote, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PawaPay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;_651c1b54 _6e226a26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve financial access in Africa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being part of an amazing team that shapes company’s culture as a great place to be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ambitious, talented, and diverse team who always has your back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We grow fast, and you will grow fast with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive remuneration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;35 days of paid leave per year (inclusive of public holidays) and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is PawaPay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PawaPay is a pan-African fintech enabling local payment channels used by the mass market to both local and international merchants. We operate in a highly regulated, partner-driven environment and are in scale-up mode, with ambitious growth plans across multiple African markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to simplify business for companies and consumers in Africa and we do that by ensuring that payments simply work, at scale, despite fragmentation and complexity that exists on the Continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our payments API we already facilitate over 4 million transactions a day across 20 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa.&amp;nbsp; We are the largest PSP on the Continent for the processing of mobile money payments, and have positioned ourselves well to lead the payment space as it grows over the next decade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PawaPay, there is an entrepreneurial spirit coupled with a modern and professional working culture. The fast-paced, ever-changing environment will suit someone who can adapt and think on their feet. In return, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a group of dedicated and smart individuals working towards the same mission. We work as a remote team and have team members in Europe, Africa and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location &amp;amp; Eligibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants &lt;strong&gt;must be n&lt;/strong&gt;ationals of a WAEMU/UEMOA member state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a remote position, we strongly prefer candidates currently based within WAEMU/UEMOA, particularly in countries where PawaPay already operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Cybersecurity Officer for West Africa, you will be responsible for executing PawaPay&#39;s cybersecurity programme across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Cybersecurity, you will serve as PawaPay&#39;s primary cybersecurity representative across Francophone and Anglophone West Africa. You will implement the company&#39;s global cybersecurity strategy while ensuring security controls, regulatory requirements and operational practices are effectively applied within the regional context.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on operational role requiring someone who is equally comfortable discussing technical security issues with Engineering teams as they are supporting regulators, auditors and business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own day-to-day regional cybersecurity activities, coordinate security operations, drive remediation of security risks and audit findings, and ensure cybersecurity remains embedded within the way pawaPay operates across West Africa.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;1219&quot; data-end=&quot;1230&quot;&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1231&quot; data-end=&quot;1262&quot;&gt;USD 30,000–45,000 per annum&lt;/strong&gt;, depending on experience, skills and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute PawaPay&#39;s cybersecurity programme across West African operations in line with the company&#39;s global cybersecurity strategy and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct security risk assessments, vulnerability reviews and security control assessments, ensuring risks are prioritised and practical remediation plans are implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate regional security incident response activities, working closely with Engineering and Operations teams to investigate, contain and remediate security issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive timely remediation of vulnerabilities, penetration test findings, audit actions and security risks by working cross-functionally with Engineering, Product, Operations and Compliance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory engagements, security audits and compliance reviews with central banks, regulators, cybersecurity authorities and data protection authorities across Francophone and Anglophone West Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regional adoption of pawaPay&#39;s security policies, standards and control frameworks while adapting implementation to local regulatory requirements where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary cybersecurity point of contact across West Africa, providing practical guidance to internal stakeholders and building trusted relationships across technical and non-technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate third-party security assessments, penetration tests and security reviews, ensuring findings are tracked through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regional security awareness initiatives and promote a strong security culture across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the evolving cybersecurity and regulatory landscape across West Africa, identifying emerging risks and recommending appropriate improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are a Great Fit If You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years&#39; experience in cybersecurity, information security or IT security within fintech, telecommunications, banking or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in both English and French (written and spoken). This is essential for supporting our Francophone West Africa operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience implementing and applying recognised security frameworks such as ISO 27001, NIST, PCI-DSS or similar within regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with vulnerability management, security incident response, security monitoring and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting security audits, regulatory reviews or compliance assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mobile money ecosystems, payment infrastructure, API-driven platforms or financial services technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with security technologies such as SIEM, EDR, vulnerability management platforms or similar security tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence Engineering, Product and Operations teams and drive security improvements without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to translate technical risks into clear, business-focused recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Information Technology or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CEH, ISO 27001 Lead Auditor/Implementer or equivalent are advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success in this Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first year you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become the trusted cybersecurity point of contact across West Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully support regulatory, audit and compliance engagements with minimal escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive timely closure of security vulnerabilities, penetration test findings and audit actions across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships with Engineering, Operations, Product, Compliance and Regulatory teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen pawaPay&#39;s cybersecurity posture by ensuring regional risks are proactively identified, prioritised and remediated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PawaPay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;_651c1b54 _6e226a26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve financial access in Africa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being part of an amazing team that shapes company’s culture as a great place to be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ambitious, talented, and diverse team who always has your back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We grow fast, and you will grow fast with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive remuneration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;35 days of paid leave per year (inclusive of public holidays) and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is PawaPay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PawaPay is a pan-African fintech enabling local payment channels used by the mass market to both local and international merchants. We operate in a highly regulated, partner-driven environment and are in scale-up mode, with ambitious growth plans across multiple African markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to simplify business for companies and consumers in Africa and we do that by ensuring that payments simply work, at scale, despite fragmentation and complexity that exists on the Continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our payments API we already facilitate over 4 million transactions a day across 20 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa.&amp;nbsp; We are the largest PSP on the Continent for the processing of mobile money payments, and have positioned ourselves well to lead the payment space as it grows over the next decade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PawaPay, there is an entrepreneurial spirit coupled with a modern and professional working culture. The fast-paced, ever-changing environment will suit someone who can adapt and think on their feet. In return, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a group of dedicated and smart individuals working towards the same mission. We work as a remote team and have team members in Europe, Africa and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As PawaPay continues to expand across multiple markets in East and Southern Africa, maintaining rigorous financial records and audit readiness is critical. We are seeking a hands-on &lt;strong&gt;Temporary Finance &amp;amp; Reconciliations Accountant for a 6-month period &lt;/strong&gt;to focus on complex, high-volume reconciliations, balance sheet clean-up, and audit preparation ahead of our upcoming FY2026 statutory audits.The role owns the execution of wallet balance reconciliations, tax GL-to-return matching, transfer pricing intercompany reconciliations, and general balance sheet substantiation. Working closely with the Finance, Tax, Treasury, and Operations teams, the person in this role will investigate historical differences, clear outstanding items, and maintain audit-ready supporting files.This is a standalone, task-focused execution role reporting into the Finance Manager.&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;This is not an FP&amp;amp;A, business partnering, or strategic controller role.&lt;/em&gt; It is a dedicated, detail-heavy reconciliation engine built for an accountant who enjoys digging into complex transactional data and solving root-cause discrepancies.&amp;nbsp;You will inherit existing multi-country entity ledgers, historical wallet and tax reconciliation backlogs, and active audit timelines. You will work directly with our accounting and operational records to bring every schedule up to high-quality audit standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you are accountable for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The single thing this role is accountable for is &lt;strong&gt;ensuring complete, accurate, and audit-ready financial reconciliations and balance sheet substantiation across assigned African markets. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating Principle:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Investigate, reconcile, document, clear, and substantiate.&lt;/em&gt; The Temporary Finance Accountant digs into root causes, chases down historical discrepancies, and builds complete supporting schedules. Strategic tax planning, regulatory interpretations, group treasury decisions, and final sign-off on tax returns and financial statements belong to Finance Leadership.What you are not accountable for: Group tax strategy, treasury allocation, statutory sign-offs, and broad financial planning &amp;amp; analysis (owned by the Tax Manager, Treasury Lead, and Finance Leadership).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you own day to day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wallet Reconciliations.&lt;/strong&gt; Perform historical and current reconciliations of customer wallet balances against general ledger accounts and operational MNO data, investigating unmatched transactions and maintaining clear aged schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax GL-to-Return Reconciliations.&lt;/strong&gt; Reconcile tax balances (VAT, Withholding Tax, and local statutory taxes) recorded in the general ledger against filed returns across assigned markets, investigating variances and substantiating tax liabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transfer Pricing &amp;amp; Intercompany Matching.&lt;/strong&gt; Execute transfer pricing reconciliations for entities operating under local invoicing arrangements, matching revenue, intercompany charges, and service/technical fees against agreed transfer pricing calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit PBC &amp;amp; Schedule Preparation.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain complete audit schedules, working papers, and supporting documentation required for FY2026 statutory audits and the Q1 2027 audit cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Query &amp;amp; Request Coordination.&lt;/strong&gt; Track open external auditor PBC requests, retrieve supporting evidence, follow up with internal teams, and resolve prior-period balance sheet queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance Sheet Substantiation.&lt;/strong&gt; Perform month-end and year-end balance sheet substantiation, actively driving down aged or unsupported items across multi-country entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 2 to 4 years of hands-on accounting or finance experience, with a proven track record in balance sheet reconciliations, tax matching, and general ledger maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Qualifications.&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or Commerce. Progress toward or completion of CPA, ACCA, or an equivalent professional qualification is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Background.&lt;/strong&gt; Previous experience within fintech, payments, banking, financial services, or audit environments handling high-volume transactional data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excel Proficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced skills in Microsoft Excel (data manipulation, complex lookups, reconciliation formulas, and pivot tables). Familiarity with Xero or modern cloud accounting software is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Rigor.&lt;/strong&gt; An investigative mindset focused on identifying root causes of historical differences rather than simply highlighting variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location.&lt;/strong&gt; Candidates must be based in &lt;strong&gt;Nairobi (Kenya)&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Tanzania&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PawaPay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;_651c1b54 _6e226a26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve financial access in Africa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being part of an amazing team that shapes company’s culture as a great place to be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ambitious, talented, and diverse team who always has your back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We grow fast, and you will grow fast with us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive remuneration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;35 days of paid leave per year (inclusive of public holidays) and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is PawaPay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PawaPay is a pan-African fintech enabling local payment channels used by the mass market to both local and international merchants. We operate in a highly regulated, partner-driven environment and are in scale-up mode, with ambitious growth plans across multiple African markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to simplify business for companies and consumers in Africa and we do that by ensuring that payments simply work, at scale, despite fragmentation and complexity that exists on the Continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our payments API we already facilitate over 4 million transactions a day across 20 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa.&amp;nbsp; We are the largest PSP on the Continent for the processing of mobile money payments, and have positioned ourselves well to lead the payment space as it grows over the next decade.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PawaPay, there is an entrepreneurial spirit coupled with a modern and professional working culture. The fast-paced, ever-changing environment will suit someone who can adapt and think on their feet. In return, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a group of dedicated and smart individuals working towards the same mission. We work as a remote team and have team members in Europe, Africa and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;the-opportunity&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;8dd1837b-ec8a-4038-bd1b-9edb6899a3d4&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a People and Talent team whose impact grows as PawaPay scales, with everyone focused on the value they bring and automation taking care of process and admin. This new role owns the employee experience across the lifecycle, the platforms and data that run it, and the reward, engagement and performance frameworks that shape how people experience working here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role and a senior individual contributor one. You&#39;ll be the design engine behind how people experience PawaPay: career conversations that help people grow, the way managers give feedback, the behaviours we expect from leaders as we scale. Some of it you&#39;ll build yourself, and some you&#39;ll get built with colleagues. We want someone who loves building automations, agents and workflows, and would happily ship one this week and improve it next week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll inherit strong foundations and a close-knit team, partnering with our People and Talent Coordinator (who owns onboarding) and our Ops and Exec Support Lead on day-to-day operations. Overall people strategy sits with the Head of People and Talent; recruitment, hiring workflows and the recruitment platform sit with the Talent Lead. Much of what you&#39;ll own is being designed as we go, and team growth will follow evidence of need. You&#39;ll also give ad hoc in-country support, such as office help or events, where you&#39;re based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-own&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI and automation.&lt;/strong&gt; Design, build and maintain automations, workflows and AI agents across our people platforms, from simple triggered workflows to internal agents that answer employees&#39; regular questions. You set the standard for how People and Talent works AI-first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platforms and data.&lt;/strong&gt; Own our people platforms and the data layer beneath them. Connect them following our recent review, keep data clean and build guardrails (validation rules, alerts, review steps) that catch errors before they reach payroll or compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the journey through development, internal moves and offboarding, connecting seamlessly with onboarding. Set the longer-term strategy for how the employee experience evolves across every market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and levelling.&lt;/strong&gt; Run our comp and levelling process end to end, and partner with the Head of People and Talent on comp philosophy and job architecture. Deliver robust market mapping, a real-time view of total reward for everyone, and training so managers deliver comp outcomes with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement and performance.&lt;/strong&gt; Run our flagship engagement surveys and make sure they produce action leaders follow through on. Analyse performance data in aggregate, help evolve how we recognise and reward performance, and equip managers for strong performance and career conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key moments and complex contracts.&lt;/strong&gt; Support managers and employees through parental leave, bereavement, relocation, underperformance and harder casework, drawing on specialist counsel where needed. Keep policies current across markets, and template and automate our more complex employment contracts in one secure place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture and training.&lt;/strong&gt; Build rituals, processes and moments that carry our values into a remote team of 160 and beyond. Design and deliver training that improves key experiences across the lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-success-looks-like&quot;&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within your first 12 months, success will look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manual work removed.&lt;/strong&gt; Measurable hours of admin automated or eliminated, processes moved off spreadsheets and workarounds into our platforms, and an employee help agent people actually use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connected, trusted data.&lt;/strong&gt; Our people platforms are integrated, with guardrails catching errors before they reach payroll or compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward delivered well.&lt;/strong&gt; Comp cycles run on time, pay sits within bands, and managers feel confident having comp conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Surveys that lead to change.&lt;/strong&gt; Survey commitments are delivered on time, and the scores they targeted are moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A better experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Employee and leaver feedback improves, and managers feel well supported through complex people situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-were-looking-for&quot;&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;what-youll-bring&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle experience at pace.&lt;/strong&gt; Significant experience across the employee lifecycle in a fast-growing, international business, ideally remote-first and multi-jurisdiction. You can point to experiences you&#39;ve designed or improved and the difference they made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A builder&#39;s instinct with AI and platforms.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve owned HR platforms and made them work together, and you build automations, agents and workflows yourself, using tools like Claude day to day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; Highly numerate and comfortable building your own analysis to spot where the experience breaks down, make the case for change and show whether it worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on reward.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve built or evolved job architecture, run market benchmarking and delivered comp cycles, and you talk openly about pay with managers and employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People partnering across jurisdictions.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve coached managers through performance conversations and sensitive situations, with working knowledge of employment practice in several countries, including drafting and managing contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement and training that land.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve turned survey data into action leaders followed through on, and designed training that changed how people work, with evidence to show it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;nice-to-have&quot;&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in African markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognised HR qualification in the country where you&#39;re based.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong network in the people community and a habit of bringing outside ideas in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to tick every box. If this role excites you and you can see how your experience fits, we&#39;d like to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PawaPay?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
